ore_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.408423548476871,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.055147919165657755,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.2347104157113404,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.03882790309358807,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":35.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.118039995,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":78.7,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"BrightSpire Capital, Inc. operates as a commercial real estate (CRE) credit real estate investment trust in the United States and Norway. It operates through Senior and Mezzanine Loans and Preferred Equity; Net Leased and Other Real Estate; and Corporate and Other segments. The company focuses on originating, acquiring, financing, and managing a diversified portfolio of CRE debt investments consisting of senior mortgage loans, mezzanine loans, preferred equity investments, net leased real estate and other real estate properties, and CRE debt securities. It also engages in money market activities; and invests in private equity funds. The company has elected to be taxed as a real estate investment trust. As a result, it would not be subject to federal corporate income taxes if it distributes at least 90% of its taxable income to its stockholders. The company was formerly known as Colony Credit Real Estate, Inc. and changed its name to BrightSpire Capital, Inc. in June 2021. BrightSpire Capital, Inc. was incorporated in 2017 and is based in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael Joseph Mazzei J.D. | CEO & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $2.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 46 people. Revenue per employee of $7.2M ranks in the top quartile among Real Estate peers, with revenue falling 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $1.2M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $279K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["BrightSpire Capital, Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $400M market cap on $331M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are expanding by +2.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -1% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $55M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 17 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -2.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 23.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 12% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Operating margins 41% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 50/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Real Estate peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Real Estate peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Real Estate peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"BrightSpire Capital, Inc. $BRSP Stock: Private Management Group Inc. Raises Holdings","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/brightspire-capital-inc-brsp-stock-private-management-group-inc-raises-holdings.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794307827.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.869,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"BrightSpire Capital (NYSE:BRSP) Stock Gets Price Target Trim from JonesTrading","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/31/brightspire-capital-nysebrsp-stock-gets-price-ta